1
00:00:06,410 --> 00:00:10,230
An advert says that a farm has 35 hectares of land.

2
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:13,500
To picture that, think of a football pitch.

3
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:17,170
A pitch is about 100 metres by 70 metres.

4
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:21,450
First, what is the area of the football pitch, in square metres?

5
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,000
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:29,680
100 times 70 is 7,000 square metres.

7
00:00:29,730 --> 00:00:33,260
1 hectare is 10,000 square metres.

8
00:00:33,310 --> 00:00:38,010
So 35 hectares is 350,000 square metres.

9
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:41,250
350,000 divided by 7,000 is 50.

10
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:46,190
The farm is as big as 50 football pitches.

11
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:51,440
Remember: the area of a rectangle is the length times the width.

12
00:00:51,490 --> 00:00:57,570
A field 250 metres by 80 metres has an area of 20,000 square metres.

13
00:00:57,620 --> 00:01:00,100
Land is measured in hectares.

14
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:05,350
1 hectare is the area of a square, 100 metres by 100 metres.

15
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:08,440
That is 10,000 square metres.

16
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:11,210
The short way to write hectares is h a.

17
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:14,530
A football pitch is about 0.7 hectares.

18
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:19,830
To change hectares into square metres, multiply by 10,000.

19
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:20,530
Your turn.

20
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:22,990
Change 3 hectares to square metres.

21
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:26,290
Pause the video and try it.

22
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:31,610
3 times 10,000 is 30,000 square metres.

23
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:36,870
To change square metres into hectares, divide by 10,000.

24
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:40,900
85,000 square metres is 8.5 hectares.

25
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:46,120
To find the area of a field in hectares, first find its area in square metres.

26
00:01:46,170 --> 00:01:47,480
Then divide.

27
00:01:47,530 --> 00:01:48,270
Your turn.

28
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:51,130
A field is 200 metres by 250 metres.

29
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:53,440
What is its area in hectares?

30
00:01:53,490 --> 00:01:56,980
Pause the video and try it.

31
00:01:57,030 --> 00:02:01,230
200 times 250 is 50,000 square metres.

32
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:03,130
Divide by 10,000.

33
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:06,360
The field is 5 hectares.

34
00:02:06,410 --> 00:02:07,690
Here is the method.

35
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:10,420
Step 1: find the area in square metres.

36
00:02:10,470 --> 00:02:13,070
The lengths must be in metres.

37
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:17,530
Step 2: divide by 10,000 to get hectares.

38
00:02:17,580 --> 00:02:23,700
Step 3: to go from hectares to square metres, multiply by 10,000.

39
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:26,600
Step 4: check with something you know.

40
00:02:26,650 --> 00:02:30,140
A football pitch is about 0.7 hectares.

41
00:02:30,190 --> 00:02:33,230
A field is 300 metres by 180 metres.

42
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:36,010
Find its area in hectares.

43
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:41,320
300 times 180 is 54,000 square metres.

44
00:02:41,370 --> 00:02:43,000
Divide by 10,000.

45
00:02:43,050 --> 00:02:46,130
The field is 5.4 hectares.

46
00:02:46,180 --> 00:02:50,630
A forest is a rectangle, 1.5 kilometres by 0.8 kilometres.

47
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:53,200
Find its area in hectares.

48
00:02:53,250 --> 00:02:58,320
Change to metres first: 1,500 metres by 800 metres.

49
00:02:58,370 --> 00:03:02,490
The area is 1,200,000 square metres.

50
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:04,240
Divide by 10,000.

51
00:03:04,290 --> 00:03:07,570
The forest is 120 hectares.

52
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:11,280
A rectangular field has an area of 3.6 hectares.

53
00:03:11,330 --> 00:03:12,980
It is 300 metres long.

54
00:03:13,030 --> 00:03:14,680
How wide is it?

55
00:03:14,730 --> 00:03:19,230
3.6 hectares is 36,000 square metres.

56
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:22,190
Divide the area by the length.

57
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:25,060
36,000 divided by 300 is 120.

58
00:03:25,110 --> 00:03:28,470
The field is 120 metres wide.

59
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:32,130
Land costs 6,000 dollars for each hectare.

60
00:03:32,180 --> 00:03:37,740
Find the price of a plot that is 500 metres by 140 metres.

61
00:03:37,790 --> 00:03:41,920
500 times 140 is 70,000 square metres.

62
00:03:41,970 --> 00:03:44,560
That is 7 hectares.

63
00:03:44,610 --> 00:03:49,180
7 times 6,000 is 42,000 dollars.

64
00:03:49,230 --> 00:03:52,350
Change 62,000 square metres to hectares.

65
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:54,180
Here is Yuri's working.

66
00:03:54,230 --> 00:03:56,950
Which line goes wrong first?

67
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,540
Line 1 is wrong.

68
00:03:58,590 --> 00:04:02,310
1 hectare is 100 metres by 100 metres.

69
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:06,630
That is 10,000 square metres, not 100.

70
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:12,330
62,000 divided by 10,000 is 6.2 hectares.

71
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:16,830
The smallest country in the world is Vatican City, inside Rome.

72
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:19,880
Its area is only about 44 hectares.

73
00:04:19,930 --> 00:04:22,920
That is less than half a square kilometre.

74
00:04:22,970 --> 00:04:26,710
You could walk across it in about 10 minutes.

75
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:31,380
Central Park, in New York, is much bigger: about 340 hectares.

76
00:04:31,430 --> 00:04:35,240
Almost 8 Vatican Cities would fit inside it.

77
00:04:35,290 --> 00:04:36,510
One last question.

78
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:40,020
How many hectares are there in 1 square kilometre?

79
00:04:40,070 --> 00:04:43,670
Pause the video and work it out.

80
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:51,230
1 square kilometre is 1,000 metres by 1,000 metres: 1 million square metres.

81
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:52,920
Divide by 10,000.

82
00:04:52,970 --> 00:04:55,560
That is 100 hectares.

83
00:04:55,610 --> 00:04:59,980
To remember: 1 hectare is 10,000 square metres.

84
00:05:00,030 --> 00:05:04,300
It is a square 100 metres by 100 metres.

85
00:05:04,350 --> 00:05:08,340
Square metres to hectares: divide by 10,000.

86
00:05:08,390 --> 00:05:13,110
Hectares to square metres: multiply by 10,000.

87
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:16,530
100 hectares make 1 square kilometre.

88
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:20,390
Always work out the area in square metres first.

89
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:25,830
Great work! Now practise lesson 15.2 on Camday.
